.TH 3DMOUSE-OSD 1 2026-11-10 "3dmouse-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
3dmouse-osd \- on-screen overlay for 3DMouse Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 3dmouse-osd
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draws the messages, button help and radial menus that
.BR 3dmouse-agent (1)
announces. It runs as the user service
.BR 3dmouse-osd.service .
.PP
On compositors with wlr-layer-shell (Hyprland, Sway, KDE Plasma, COSMIC) it uses overlay-layer
surfaces. On X11 it uses frameless always-on-top windows. It never takes keyboard focus, and pointer
input passes through it.
.PP
GNOME Wayland has no layer-shell. There, and in builds without LayerShellQt on Wayland, it exits
with status 0 and the agent keeps using desktop notifications.
.B 3dmousectl diagnostics check
shows which one is active.
.PP
The position (top, centre, bottom) and size are agent settings
.RB ( osd_position ", " osd_scale ),
editable in
.BR 3dmouse-config (1).
Everything is hidden while the screen is locked.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B THREEDMOUSE_AGENT_SOCKET
The agent socket path.
.TP
.B SM_OSD_FORCE
Start even where no overlay is expected (for testing).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 3dmouse-agent (1),
.BR 3dmousectl (1)
